1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,885
Adoption depends on the complete task,
incentives, confidence, and support.

2
00:00:04,955 --> 00:00:10,715
Training alone will not fix an extra queue,
unclear responsibility, or fear of punitive

3
00:00:10,785 --> 00:00:16,375
measurement. Observe the task again after
rollout and ask where the new system adds effort.

4
00:00:16,445 --> 00:00:19,346
Provide a visible override and a safe fallback.

5
00:00:19,416 --> 00:00:25,624
Plan a defined adoption period with checkpoints
and a denominator that reflects eligible work.

6
00:00:25,694 --> 00:00:30,473
Agents abandon the tool because they must
copy the result back into the main queue.

7
00:00:30,543 --> 00:00:34,297
The suggestion is accurate, but
the complete task takes longer.

8
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:38,698
Maya also discovers agents think
overrides will count against them.

9
00:00:38,768 --> 00:00:43,547
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

10
00:00:43,617 --> 00:00:47,222
Propose two workflow changes
and a small test for each.

11
00:00:47,292 --> 00:00:52,305
Test placing suggestions within the existing
review step rather than a separate queue.

12
00:00:52,375 --> 00:00:57,794
Clarify that overrides are learning evidence
during the pilot and observe whether behavior

13
00:00:57,864 --> 00:01:02,387
changes. Measure the complete task
time and eligible-ticket adoption.

14
00:01:02,457 --> 00:01:08,195
Do not infer trust from positive survey
comments alone when actual use remains low.

15
00:01:08,265 --> 00:01:11,188
Which signal most directly
shows workflow adoption?

16
00:01:11,258 --> 00:01:13,647
A. Attendance at a training session B.

17
00:01:13,717 --> 00:01:15,659
A favorable sponsor quote C.

18
00:01:15,729 --> 00:01:18,075
Sustained use in eligible tasks.

19
00:01:18,145 --> 00:01:19,553
The best answer is C.

20
00:01:19,623 --> 00:01:21,223
Attendance is an input.

21
00:01:21,293 --> 00:01:23,661
Actual workflow use is behavior.
